%description:

Tcp.keepAliveProbeCount:zero -- the connection aborts after 0 unanswered probes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the keepalive probes without an answer, after which the connection
aborts (Linux tcp_keepalive_probes; RFC 9293 MUST-29: one probe without an answer is not a
dead connection)".

The classes: linux (9, the default, the value of Linux tcp_keepalive_probes), other (another
count), zero (0: the connection aborts at the idle time, without a probe). The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::processKeepAliveTimer() aborts the connection when the probes without an
answer reach the value, at the expiry of the timer after the last probe. This test separates "zero" from the other values.

Host under test: host1, with keepalive, an idle time of 1 s and an interval of 1 s
(preconditions); host1 sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s and then nothing; host2 sends nothing. A keepalive probe is a
segment without data with SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1. The tap drops each segment of host2 after the data, so no probe gets an
answer. Observation: level 1 and 2, the connection goes to the state CLOSED (the signal state,
value 1) 1 s after the ACK of the data, after 0 probes.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveProbeCount
%# class: zero
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveProbeCount
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveProbeCountZero")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1: the idle time starts")
             .within(1.0))
        .meanwhile(tap("tap").from("host2").drop()
                       .describe("each segment of host2 after the data: the probes get no answer"))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("probes")
                                        .within(14.0)))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("state")
                   .filterValue(1)
                   .describe("an early abort")
                   .within(0.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("state")
                  .filterValue(1)
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp", "{probes} == 0")
                  .describe("the abort: the state CLOSED, after 0 probes")
                  .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveProbeCountZero compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveProbeCount = 0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 1s
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveInterval = 1s
sim-time-limit = 15s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveProbeCountZero: PASS
